{
  "description": "Access group/policy exclude+require rules are the same discriminated union as include, but the docs render their arms as bare one-key wrappers (e.g. `object { github-organization }` with no children), so spec-to-smithy converts them to degenerate `{ key: Document }` structures. The include arms are fully specified and Cloudflare accepts the identical rule union in all three positions - point exclude/require at the include list so the request types (and wire encoding, e.g. the `github-organization` jsonName) match the include side. Paths address the post-per-op-patch (verb-first) request roots.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/shapes/com.cloudflare.zero_trust#CreateAccessGroupForAccountRequest/members/exclude/target",
      "value": "com.cloudflare.zero_trust#AccessGroupsCreateForAccountRequestIncludeList"
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/shapes/com.cloudflare.zero_trust#CreateAccessGroupForAccountRequest/members/require/target",
      "value": "com.cloudflare.zero_trust#AccessGroupsCreateForAccountRequestIncludeList"
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/shapes/com.cloudflare.zero_trust#UpdateAccessGroupForAccountRequest/members/exclude/target",
      "value": "com.cloudflare.zero_trust#AccessGroupsUpdateForAccountRequestIncludeList"
    },
    {
